  "presentation_summary": [
    "62-year-old South Korean tourist presented in Santiago, Chile after 5 days of fever, chills, headache, myalgia, severe malaise, rash, and eschar.",
    "Exposure history included a recent farm visit south of Seoul before travel.",
    "Presentation showed fever 38.8 degC, tachycardia 108 bpm, generalized trunk-predominant maculopapular rash, and a 6 mm necrotic eschar on the posterior thigh.",
    "Laboratory findings included thrombocytopenia, mild hyponatremia, elevated CRP, transaminitis, cholestatic enzymes, and high LDH.",
    "Orientia IgM serology and real-time PCR confirmed O. tsutsugamushi Kawasaki clade; he improved rapidly with doxycycline."
  ],
